{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"PHASE 2 COMPLETE (implementation landed for review; ticket left in_progress pending CI). Both operator-approved remedies are implemented, tested OFFLINE, and pushed to Gerrit.\n\nGERRIT CHANGE: 1386 — https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1386\nLocal commit: 777e885cb6 (\"1dbe: read prompt cache across plan-review passes\"), rebar-ticket trailer present, DCO-signed, Change-Id Id60c2a5.\n\nWHAT LANDED:\n- Remedy 2 (the prize): new RunRequest.cache_prefix runner-seam knob. When set to a byte-stable proper prefix of system_prompt, agent_call.build_agent_kwargs sends the prefix as the static system_prompt and the REMAINDER as a zero-arg DYNAMIC instruction — pydantic-ai's anthropic/bedrock cache-instructions then place the breakpoint at the PREFIX boundary (they mark the last STATIC block). Model still receives prefix+remainder byte-identically; only the cache boundary moves. Wired into the Pass-1 finder (passes.py, cache_prefix=shared_plan_prefix(plan)) so it WRITES at the shared boundary, and into every verify step via workflow/runs.build_agent_request (reads ctx.inputs[\"shared_prefix\"]) so the Pass-2 verifiers READ that write within one run. Prerequisite-verifier template reordered to LEAD with {{shared_prefix}} (dropped its trailing {{plan}} block, whose bytes the prefix already carries); prerequisite_workflow_ops + its output schema + plan-review.yaml pass shared_prefix through.\n- Remedy 1 (AC4 telemetry): structured_run.cache_write_never_read + warn_if_cache_write_never_read detect the write-every-call/read-0 run shape; usage_log.summarize calls it over the run's rows. The per-call warn_if_cache_ineffective (write==0 AND read==0) could never see this shape.\n\nTESTS (offline, no live LLM):\n- NEW tests/unit/test_cache_prefix_breakpoint.py (10): breakpoint-boundary proof against REAL pydantic-ai _map_message (anthropic) / _map_messages (bedrock) — cache_control/cachePoint lands exactly on the shared prefix block; plus the write>0/read==0 telemetry detector/warn and no-op guards (no cache_prefix, non-proper-prefix ignored).\n- tests/unit/workflow/test_shared_prefix.py +3: prereq-verifier now LEADS with shared_plan_prefix, no stance/plan content lost by the reorder (fidelity check), and verify-inputs emits shared_prefix.\n- Updated test_plan_review_prerequisites_heldout for the new shared_prefix output key.\n- Regression: full llm/plan_review/prerequisite/cache/prompt/usage/runner sweep green (1445 passed). The only failures in the tree are pre-existing test_web_tool_gating cases that ImportError on the missing ddgs/duckduckgo_search dep — identical on origin/main, unrelated to this change.\n\nGATES: make lint clean; make typecheck clean (mypy, 430 files); module-size cap respected — passes.py at exactly 800/800 (consolidated three function-local `from ...prompting import prompts` imports to one module-level import to make room for the finder cache_prefix line). Live A/B skipped per operator direction: the hit is proven by the offline breakpoint-boundary test + the byte-identical-prefix render alignment.\n\nAC RE-SCOPE: the \"byte-identical marked prefix across TICKETS\" AC remains WITHDRAWN as unsatisfiable (see the Phase-2 comment above and investigation (b).2/(c).3), replaced by the achievable breakpoint-at-shared-prefix-boundary AC, which the offline tests pin.\n\nCLOSE DECISION: LEFT IN_PROGRESS. Per AGENTS.md the change must reach Verified +1 (green CI) AND LLM-Review +1 before Submit, and a ticket is not closed until its change is Verified +1 — a passing completion-verifier is not a substitute for green CI. Change 1386 was just pushed and has neither vote yet, so closing now would force past a not-yet-green gate. Will close after 1386 merges (Verified +1 + LLM-Review +1 + Submit)."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785869495458255001,"uuid":"460cffa9-3548-42c4-9c78-7e470901aab7"}